Context:
- `--max-time 20sec` is required because the API host sometimes accepts a connection and never responds.
- The releases API returns entries in no particular order, so the script must sort them itself.
- Tags that do not start with `v` are nightly builds and should not trigger notifications.
- The state file stores the latest announced tag and is updated only after printing, so a crash between printing and saving will re-announce that release on the next run.

```nu
def main [repo: string, state_file: string] {
  let releases = (http get --max-time 20sec $"https://api.example.com/repos/($repo)/releases")
  let latest = ($releases | where tag_name starts-with "v" | sort-by published_at | last)
  let seen = (if ($state_file | path exists) { open $state_file | str trim } else { "" })
  if $latest.tag_name == $seen { return }
  print $"($repo) ($latest.tag_name): ($latest.html_url)"
  $latest.tag_name | save --force $state_file
}
```

